VALUES ($q$count-islands$q$, $q$Count the Islands$q$, $q$A map is a grid of 0 (water) and 1 (land). An island is a group of land cells connected horizontally or vertically (diagonals do not connect). Count the islands.$q$, $q$Medium$q$, $q$Graphs$q$, 'code', ARRAY[$q$graph$q$, $q$bfs$q$, $q$dfs$q$, $q$grid$q$]::text[], $q${"python": "import sys\n\n\ndef main():\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().split('\\n')\n    # Input:\n    # Line 1: R and C.\n    # Next R lines: each a string of C characters, 0 or 1, with no spaces.\n    # TODO: solve, then print the answer\n\n\nmain()\n", "javascript": "const lines = require('fs').readFileSync(0, 'utf8').split('\\n');\n// Input:\n// Line 1: R and C.\n// Next R lines: each a string of C characters, 0 or 1, with no spaces.\n// TODO: solve, then console.log the answer\n", "java": "import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String s; (s = in.readLine()) != null; ) lines.add(s);\n        // Input:\n        // Line 1: R and C.\n        // Next R lines: each a string of C characters, 0 or 1, with no spaces.\n        // TODO: solve, then System.out.println the answer\n    }\n}\n", "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    // Input:\n    // Line 1: R and C.\n    // Next R lines: each a string of C characters, 0 or 1, with no spaces.\n    // TODO: read with cin / getline, solve, print the answer\n    return 0;\n}\n", "c": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    // Input:\n    // Line 1: R and C.\n    // Next R lines: each a string of C characters, 0 or 1, with no spaces.\n    /* TODO: read with scanf / fgets, solve, print the answer */\n    return 0;\n}\n"}$q$::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, $q$[{"input": "4 5\n11000\n11000\n00100\n00011", "output": "3", "explanation": "Top-left block, the single middle cell, and the bottom-right pair."}, {"input": "3 3\n101\n010\n101", "output": "5", "explanation": "Diagonal neighbours are separate islands."}]$q$::jsonb, ARRAY[$q$1 ≤ R, C ≤ 220$q$]::text[], 25, 1011, 2000, 262144, $q$Line 1: R and C.
Next R lines: each a string of C characters, 0 or 1, with no spaces.$q$, $q$One integer, the number of islands.$q$, $q$Scan every cell. When you meet unvisited land, count one island and flood-fill it (BFS or DFS) so its cells are marked visited. Use an explicit stack or queue instead of recursion, because a snake-shaped island can be tens of thousands of cells deep. O(R·C).$q$, false)
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

